\subsection*{Compilation Instructions}
All documents compile using standard \LaTeX\ engines:

\begin{verbatim}
pdflatex aegis_continuum.tex
bibtex   aegis_continuum
pdflatex aegis_continuum.tex
pdflatex aegis_continuum.tex
\end{verbatim}

The white paper requires \texttt{amsmath}, \texttt{amssymb},
\texttt{amsthm}, and \texttt{geometry}. No external images or figures
are required.

\subsection*{Extending the Documentation}
Researchers may extend the documentation by adding new sections under
\texttt{sections/}. All additions must follow the established
structure:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Formal definitions of operators and tensors
    \item Variational or geometric derivations
    \item Theorem statements with complete proofs
    \item Reduction to known physical limits
    \item Numerical or empirical validation pathways
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Citation Format}
All references should be added to \texttt{references.bib} and cited
using standard Bib\TeX\ commands:

\begin{verbatim}
\cite{einstein1915}, \cite{landau_lifshitz}, \cite{mhd_review}
\end{verbatim}

\subsection*{Versioning}
Major revisions should increment the version number in the main
document header:

\begin{verbatim}
\def\AEGISVersion{v1.0.0}
\end{verbatim}

